IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`

-- LAYER 1: section 2025(a) and (b): administrative cost-sharing, and work supplementation or support programs
-- (7 U.S.C. 2025; lines 1911-1932 of usc07-ch51.txt, a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text).
-- Money is a NUMBER of dollars; a share is a fraction (50 percent is 0.50).
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / JUST n is what the text says, NOTHING is "not covered" (NOTES.md, Reading a result).

-- s 2025(a): the nine kinds of cost the text lists, the one it takes out, and everything else.
DECLARE `s 2025(a) cost` IS ONE OF
    `s 2025(a)(1) certification of applicant households`
    `s 2025(a)(2) acceptance, storage, protection, control, and accounting of benefits after delivery to receiving points within the State`
    `s 2025(a)(3) issuance of benefits to all eligible households`
    `s 2025(a)(4) informational activities relating to the program`
    `s 2025(a)(4) recruitment activities to persuade an individual to apply, or promotion of the program on television, radio, or billboards`
    `s 2025(a)(5) fair hearings`
    `s 2025(a)(6) automated data processing and information retrieval systems`
    `s 2025(a)(7) investigations and prosecutions`
    `s 2025(a)(8) implementing and operating the immigration status verification system`
    `s 2025(a)(9) establishing and operating a longitudinal database`
    `s 2025(a) any other cost`

-- s 2025(a), the retention proviso: what the Secretary may permit a State to keep of what it recovers or collects.
DECLARE `s 2025(a) retention` IS ONE OF
    `s 2025(a) may be permitted to retain` HAS `share` IS A NUMBER
    `s 2025(a) may not be permitted to retain under this proviso`

§ `s 2025(a) Administrative costs`

-- UNIT: the share is a FRACTION, not the percent printed in the text: 50 percent is 0.50 and 25 percent is 0.25 (every share and rate of this module is a fraction).
-- src:1913 | Subject to subsection (k), the Secretary is authorized to pay to each State agency, through fiscal year 2026, 50 percent, and for fiscal year 2027 and each fiscal year thereafter, 25 percent,
@ref s 2025(a) 50 percent through fiscal year 2026, 25 percent after (src:1913)
GIVEN `fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2025(a) the share of administrative costs the Secretary is authorized to pay` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `fiscal year` AT MOST 2026 THEN JUST 0.50
        IF `fiscal year` AT LEAST 2027 THEN JUST 0.25
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states a share through fiscal year 2026 and from fiscal year 2027, and no share for a number that is neither (a year that is not a whole number)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Before any reduction under subsection (k): the share TIMES the administrative costs.
@ref s 2025(a) all administrative costs involved in each State agency's operation (src:1913)
GIVEN `fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      `administrative costs in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2025(a) the amount the Secretary is authorized to pay before any reduction under subsection (k)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2025(a) the share of administrative costs the Secretary is authorized to pay` `fiscal year`
    WHEN JUST share THEN JUST (`administrative costs in dollars` TIMES share)
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 2025(a) states no share for that fiscal year
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1913 | which costs shall include, but not be limited to, the cost of (1) the certification of applicant households, (2) the acceptance, storage, protection, control, and accounting of benefits after their delivery to receiving points within the State, (3) the issuance of benefits to all eligible households, (4) informational activities relating to the supplemental nutrition assistance program, including those undertaken under section 2020(e)(1)(A) of this title, but not including recruitment activities designed to persuade an individual to apply for program benefits or that promote the program through television, radio, or billboard advertisements, (5) fair hearings, (6) automated data processing and information retrieval systems subject to the conditions set forth in subsection (g), (7) supplemental nutrition assistance program investigations and prosecutions, (8) implementing and operating the immigration status verification system established under section 1137(d) of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 1320b–7(d)), and (9) establishing and operating a longitudinal database in accordance with section 2026(n) of this title
@ref s 2025(a)(1)-(9) the costs (src:1913)
GIVEN cost IS A `s 2025(a) cost`
      `the conditions set forth in subsection (g) are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(a) the cost is an administrative cost the Secretary is authorized to pay a share of` MEANS
    CONSIDER cost
    WHEN `s 2025(a)(4) recruitment activities to persuade an individual to apply, or promotion of the program on television, radio, or billboards` THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but not including recruitment activities designed to persuade an individual to apply for program benefits or that promote the program through television, radio, or billboard advertisements"
        JUST FALSE
    WHEN `s 2025(a)(6) automated data processing and information retrieval systems` THEN
        CONSIDER `the conditions set forth in subsection (g) are met`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to the conditions set forth in subsection (g)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "which costs shall include, but not be limited to" the nine listed
    WHEN `s 2025(a) any other cost` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1913 | Provided, That the Secretary is authorized at the Secretary’s discretion to pay any State agency administering the supplemental nutrition assistance program on all or part of an Indian reservation under section 2020(d) of this title or in a Native village within the State of Alaska identified in section 1610(b) of title 43, such amounts for administrative costs as the Secretary determines to be necessary for effective operation of the supplemental nutrition assistance program
@ref s 2025(a) proviso: reservations and Native villages (src:1913)
GIVEN `the State agency administers the program on all or part of an Indian reservation under section 2020(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency administers the program in a Native village within the State of Alaska identified in section 1610(b) of title 43` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount the Secretary determines necessary for effective operation, in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2025(a) the additional amount the Secretary may pay a State agency for a reservation or a Native village` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency administers the program on all or part of an Indian reservation under section 2020(d)`
            OR `the State agency administers the program in a Native village within the State of Alaska identified in section 1610(b) of title 43`
        THEN `the amount the Secretary determines necessary for effective operation, in dollars`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the discretion is "to pay any State agency administering the supplemental nutrition assistance program on all or part of an Indian reservation ... or in a Native village"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- "pursuant to sections 2015(b) and 2022(c)" is read as either section (fork F-3 in NOTES.md); "except" is read as qualifying only the
-- 20 percent limb ("any other funds"), the nearest antecedent (fork F-3).
-- src:1913 | as well as to permit each State to retain 35 percent of the value of all funds or allotments recovered or collected pursuant to sections 2015(b) and 2022(c) of this title and 20 percent of the value of any other funds or allotments recovered or collected, except the value of funds or allotments recovered or collected that arise from an error of a State agency
@ref s 2025(a) the State may retain 35 percent or 20 percent (src:1913)
GIVEN `recovered or collected pursuant to section 2015(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `recovered or collected pursuant to section 2022(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `arises from an error of a State agency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 2025(a) retention`
`s 2025(a) the share of recovered or collected funds the Secretary may permit the State to retain` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `recovered or collected pursuant to section 2015(b)` OR `recovered or collected pursuant to section 2022(c)` THEN `s 2025(a) may be permitted to retain` 0.35
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "20 percent of the value of any other funds or allotments recovered or collected, except the value of funds or allotments recovered or collected that arise from an error of a State agency"
        IF `arises from an error of a State agency` THEN `s 2025(a) may not be permitted to retain under this proviso`
        OTHERWISE `s 2025(a) may be permitted to retain` 0.20

-- src:1913 | permit each State to retain 35 percent of the value of all funds or allotments recovered or collected pursuant to sections 2015(b) and 2022(c) of this title and 20 percent of the value of any other funds or allotments recovered or collected, except the value of funds or allotments recovered or collected that arise from an error of a State agency
@ref s 2025(a) the part of a claim the State may retain (src:1913)
GIVEN `claim` IS A Claim
      `recovered or collected pursuant to section 2015(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `recovered or collected pursuant to section 2022(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `arises from an error of a State agency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2025(a) the amount of the claim the State may be permitted to retain, in dollars` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2025(a) the share of recovered or collected funds the Secretary may permit the State to retain` `recovered or collected pursuant to section 2015(b)` `recovered or collected pursuant to section 2022(c)` `arises from an error of a State agency`
    WHEN `s 2025(a) may be permitted to retain` share THEN claim's `amount in dollars` TIMES share
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except the value of funds or allotments recovered or collected that arise from an error of a State agency"
    WHEN `s 2025(a) may not be permitted to retain under this proviso` THEN 0

-- src:1913 | The officials responsible for making determinations of ineligibility under this chapter shall not receive or benefit from revenues retained by the State under the provisions of this subsection.
@ref s 2025(a) officials shall not benefit from retained revenues (src:1913)
GIVEN `the official is responsible for making determinations of ineligibility under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(a) the official may receive or benefit from the revenues retained by the State` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not receive or benefit from revenues retained by the State under the provisions of this subsection"
        IF `the official is responsible for making determinations of ineligibility under this chapter` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on "the officials responsible for making determinations of ineligibility under this chapter"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2025(b) Work supplementation or support program`

-- src:1916 | In this subsection, the term “work supplementation or support program” means a program under which, as determined by the Secretary, public assistance (including any benefits provided under a program established by the State and the supplemental nutrition assistance program) is provided to an employer to be used for hiring and employing a public assistance recipient who was not employed by the employer at the time the public assistance recipient entered the program.
@ref s 2025(b)(1) work supplementation or support program defined (src:1916)
GIVEN `public assistance is provided to an employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to be used for hiring and employing a public assistance recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recipient was not employed by the employer when the recipient entered the program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary determines the program is one under which that is so` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(b)(1) the program is a work supplementation or support program` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a program under which"
        IF (NOT (`public assistance is provided to an employer` AND `it is to be used for hiring and employing a public assistance recipient` AND `the recipient was not employed by the employer when the recipient entered the program`)) THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the Secretary determines the program is one under which that is so`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as determined by the Secretary"
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Secretary's determination was not supplied
            OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1918 | A State agency may elect to use an amount equal to the allotment that would otherwise be issued to a household under the supplemental nutrition assistance program, but for the operation of this subsection, for the purpose of subsidizing or supporting a job under a work supplementation or support program established by the State.
@ref s 2025(b)(2) the State agency may elect (src:1918)
GIVEN `the job is under a work supplementation or support program established by the State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(b)(2) the State agency may elect to use an amount equal to the allotment to subsidize or support the job` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the job is under a work supplementation or support program established by the State` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purpose of subsidizing or supporting a job under a work supplementation or support program established by the State"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1920 | If a State agency makes an election under paragraph (2) and identifies each household that participates in the supplemental nutrition assistance program that contains an individual who is participating in the work supplementation or support program—
@ref s 2025(b)(3) procedure applies if the State agency elects and identifies (src:1920)
GIVEN `the State agency makes an election under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it identifies each household that participates in the program that contains an individual participating in the work supplementation or support program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(b)(3) the procedure applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency makes an election under paragraph (2)` AND `it identifies each household that participates in the program that contains an individual participating in the work supplementation or support program` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a State agency makes an election under paragraph (2) and identifies each household"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:1921 | (A) the Secretary shall pay to the State agency an amount equal to the value of the allotment that the household would be eligible to receive but for the operation of this subsection;
@ref s 2025(b)(3)(A) the Secretary shall pay the State agency (src:1921)
GIVEN `the procedure applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `value of the allotment the household would be eligible to receive but for the operation of this subsection, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2025(b)(3)(A) the amount the Secretary shall pay the State agency` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the procedure applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST `value of the allotment the household would be eligible to receive but for the operation of this subsection, in dollars`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty arises only "If a State agency makes an election under paragraph (2) and identifies each household"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1922 | (B) the State agency shall expend the amount received under subparagraph (A) in accordance with the work supplementation or support program in lieu of providing the allotment that the household would receive but for the operation of this subsection;
@ref s 2025(b)(3)(B) the State agency shall expend the amount (src:1922)
GIVEN `the procedure applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `amount received under subparagraph (A), in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `amount expended in accordance with the work supplementation or support program in lieu of providing the allotment, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(b)(3)(B) the State agency has expended the amount as required` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the procedure applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `amount expended in accordance with the work supplementation or support program in lieu of providing the allotment, in dollars` AT LEAST `amount received under subparagraph (A), in dollars` THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the State agency shall expend the amount received under subparagraph (A) in accordance with the work supplementation or support program"
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty arises only where the election is made and the households identified
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

