-- src:1928 | No individual shall be excused, by reason of the fact that a State has a work supplementation or support program, from any work requirement under section 2015(d) of this title, except during the periods in which the individual is employed under the work supplementation or support program.
@ref s 2025(b)(4) no excuse from a work requirement (src:1928)
GIVEN `the State has a work supplementation or support program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is employed under the work supplementation or support program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(b)(4) the individual is excused from a work requirement under section 2015(d) by reason of the fact that the State has a work supplementation or support program` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is "by reason of the fact that a State has a work supplementation or support program"
        IF (NOT `the State has a work supplementation or support program`) THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "except during the periods in which the individual is employed under the work supplementation or support program"; whether the work requirement then applies is for section 2015(d)
        IF `the individual is employed under the work supplementation or support program` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No individual shall be excused, by reason of the fact that a State has a work supplementation or support program, from any work requirement under section 2015(d)"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:1930 | A State agency shall provide a description of how the public assistance recipients in the program shall, within a specific period of time, be moved from supplemented or supported employment to employment that is not supplemented or supported.
@ref s 2025(b)(5) length of participation (src:1930)
GIVEN `the State agency has provided a description` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it says how the recipients shall, within a specific period of time, be moved to employment that is not supplemented or supported` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(b)(5) the State agency has provided the description required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency has provided a description` AND `it says how the recipients shall, within a specific period of time, be moved to employment that is not supplemented or supported` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A State agency shall provide a description of how the public assistance recipients in the program shall, within a specific period of time, be moved"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:1932 | A work supplementation or support program shall not displace the employment of individuals who are not supplemented or supported.
@ref s 2025(b)(6) displacement (src:1932)
GIVEN `the program displaces the employment of individuals who are not supplemented or supported` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(b)(6) the work supplementation or support program is permitted` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A work supplementation or support program shall not displace the employment of individuals who are not supplemented or supported"
        IF `the program displaces the employment of individuals who are not supplemented or supported` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text bars displacement and does not itself permit a program that does not displace
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
